exp="In the registry shown in the pediatric cardiology lecture (1,435 cases): <b>hypertrophic cardiomyopathy about 36%</b>, then <b>congenital coronary artery anomalies about 17%</b> (classically the left main arising from the right sinus, coursing between the aorta and pulmonary artery, compressed during exertion), followed by arrhythmogenic right ventricular cardiomyopathy (ARVC), myocarditis, mitral valve prolapse and others. Basketball was the sport most often involved, and automated external defibrillators (AEDs) at sporting events save lives.<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> The leading causes of sudden death in young athletes are hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, then coronary artery anomalies.",
