exp="Lecture's ranges:<br>• <b>Dilated</b>: ejection fraction <b>under 40%</b> — low contractility, systolic dysfunction, eccentric hypertrophy.<br>• <b>Hypertrophic</b>: <b>50–80%</b>, often hyperdynamic — diastolic dysfunction with asymmetric septal hypertrophy.<br>• <b>Restrictive</b>: <b>45–90%</b>, usually normal or near-normal — diastolic dysfunction with big atria and stiff, normal-sized ventricles.<br>A dilated heart cannot pump (systolic failure); a hypertrophic or restrictive heart cannot fill (diastolic failure).<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> Dilated cardiomyopathy has a low ejection fraction; hypertrophic and restrictive cardiomyopathies have normal or high ejection fractions with diastolic failure.",
